<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indian Institutes of Technology</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1951</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as IITs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs) are a group of public engineering and technology universities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the first founded at Kharagpur in 1951 as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru">Jawaharlal Nehru</a>'s programme of building scientific and industrial capacity. Entry is through a highly competitive national examination, and their graduates have become prominent in Indian industry and in the global technology sector, especially in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indian-institutes-of-technology.jpg" alt="Indian Institutes of Technology" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vis M · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IIT_Kharagpur_2016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
